# CMX-241: every dispatched `cmx-N` branch adds its own entry to the top of the same
# `## [Unreleased]` section in CHANGELOG.md (see CONTRIBUTING.md). Two branches open at
# once collide on that exact insertion point — never a semantic conflict, since both
# entries belong, but plain 3-way merge can't tell that from two edits landing on the same
# line. `merge=union` (a driver built into git itself, no extra config needed) tells git to
# keep BOTH sides' lines on a conflicting hunk instead of raising a conflict, so the
# dispatcher's judge-worktree refresh (`_refresh_judge_worktree` in chela/dispatcher.py)
# resolves the catch-up merge automatically instead of reporting `cannot_verify` for a
# reason that has nothing to do with the PR under review.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union

# CMX-160: `git diff` calls a file binary when EITHER side holds a NUL byte, and the judge's
# sweep then cannot read its changed lines (CANNOT VERIFY). decisionsmodel.js carried a
# literal NUL (now the `\0` escape), so its history still diffs as binary without this.
# `diff` forces a text diff for the dashboard's JS sources, which are always text.
chela/dashboard/static/js/*.js diff

# CMX-177: the committed frontend build is compared BYTE for byte with a fresh one, so git
# must never rewrite its line endings (core.autocrlf would make every file read as stale).
chela/dashboard/static/app/** -text
